{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_01_ET_K3IkhZu31WkBOBu0o8gz4807","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t;; r2 F1 probe -- JVM NaN set-construction retention (fresh JVM per run,\n2\t;; clojure -M:test -n fixorder-tmp-diag-test; scratch namespace deleted at\n3\t;; delivery). count = host set size, nan = ##NaN elements retained.\n4\t;;\n5\t;;   (count (into #{} [##NaN ##NaN]))                    2 nan=2  keeps\n6\t;;   (count (into #{} [##NaN ##NaN 1]))                  3 nan=2  keeps\n7\t;;   (count (into #{} [##NaN ##NaN \"x\"]))                3 nan=2  keeps\n8\t;;   (count (into #{} [##NaN ##NaN :k]))                 3 nan=2  keeps\n9\t;;   (count (into #{} [##NaN ##NaN [1]]))                3 nan=2  keeps\n10\t;;   (count (into #{} [##NaN 1 ##NaN]))                  3 nan=2  keeps\n11\t;;   (count (into #{} [##NaN ##NaN (list '+ 'n 0)))      2 nan=1  LOSES ONE\n12\t;;   (count (into #{} [##NaN app ##NaN]))                2 nan=1  LOSES ONE (any position)\n13\t;;   (count (into #{} [app ##NaN ##NaN]))                2 nan=1  LOSES ONE\n14\t;;   (count (hash-set ##NaN ##NaN))                      1 nan=1  collapses\n15\t;;   (count (apply hash-set [##NaN ##NaN 1]))            3 nan=2  keeps\n16\t;;   (count (set [##NaN ##NaN]))                         2 nan=2  keeps\n17\t;;   (count (conj #{} ##NaN ##NaN))                      1 nan=1  collapses (persistent chain)\n18\t;;   (count (conj (into #{} [##NaN ##NaN]) app))         3 nan=2  KEEPS (chosen)\n19\t;;   (count (into (into #{} [##NaN ##NaN]) [app]))       3 nan=2  KEEPS\n20\t;;   map analogues: (assoc {} ##NaN 1 ##NaN 2)           2 nan=2  keeps (r1 map tie)\n21\t;;                  (hash-map ##NaN :l ##NaN :r)         1 nan=1  collapses\n22\t;;                  (into {} [[##NaN v] [##NaN v]])      collapses (r1 observation)\n23\t;;\n24\t;; Hash collision ruled out: (hash ##NaN) = 2146959360,\n25\t;; (hash (list '+ 'n 0)) = -1050398832. The trigger for the single-session\n26\t;; loss is the seq element itself (also (list 1) loses), not its bucket.\n27\t;;\n28\t;; Conclusion: the whole-element tie IS constructable; retention is\n29\t;; per-constructor (JVM transient/persistent/check paths differ), not a\n30\t;; map-vs-set difference. The r1 \"unconstructable\" claim was a\n31\t;; misdiagnosis: the r1 block's count assertions were calibrated to a\n32\t;; collapsed set, and their failure (3 operands, NaN root seen twice)\n33\t;; actually demonstrated retention with reordering. Reviewer F1 sustained.\n34\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"024a2da5-c785-45c9-991b-d9d054578146","uuid":"5d76eea1-d57a-41be-ae97-4fea90ac982b","timestamp":"2026-11-18T20:42:11.247Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-fixorder/collab/yang-clojure/1795033280000-fixorder-r2-evidence/fixorder-r2-nan-set-probe.md","content":";; r2 F1 probe -- JVM NaN set-construction retention (fresh JVM per run,\n;; clojure -M:test -n fixorder-tmp-diag-test; scratch namespace deleted at\n;; delivery). count = host set size, nan = ##NaN elements retained.\n;;\n;;   (count (into #{} [##NaN ##NaN]))                    2 nan=2  keeps\n;;   (count (into #{} [##NaN ##NaN 1]))                  3 nan=2  keeps\n;;   (count (into #{} [##NaN ##NaN \"x\"]))                3 nan=2  keeps\n;;   (count (into #{} [##NaN ##NaN :k]))                 3 nan=2  keeps\n;;   (count (into #{} [##NaN ##NaN [1]]))                3 nan=2  keeps\n;;   (count (into #{} [##NaN 1 ##NaN]))                  3 nan=2  keeps\n;;   (count (into #{} [##NaN ##NaN (list '+ 'n 0)))      2 nan=1  LOSES ONE\n;;   (count (into #{} [##NaN app ##NaN]))                2 nan=1  LOSES ONE (any position)\n;;   (count (into #{} [app ##NaN ##NaN]))                2 nan=1  LOSES ONE\n;;   (count (hash-set ##NaN ##NaN))                      1 nan=1  collapses\n;;   (count (apply hash-set [##NaN ##NaN 1]))            3 nan=2  keeps\n;;   (count (set [##NaN ##NaN]))                