{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_00_ET_5g1UM9TS6nA4609i9P902849","type":"tool_result","content":"85\t(defn- strictly-ascending?\n86\t  \"True when `ks` sorts strictly ascending by jing/canonical-compare: every\n87\t   adjacent pair compares negative. The strict form deliberately does NOT\n88\t   certify a tie (equal adjacent keys are equal executable content and a\n89\t   legal emitted order, but not a strictly ascending one) -- blocks that\n90\t   construct a tie assert it directly or compare against the sequence's\n91\t   own non-descending sort instead.\"\n92\t  [ks]\n93\t  (every? (fn [[a b]] (neg? (jing/canonical-compare a b)))\n94\t          (partition 2 1 ks)))\n95\t\n96\t(defn- key-literals"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"024a2da5-c785-45c9-991b-d9d054578146","uuid":"10a0b980-9153-4970-bb8b-3a121408acf7","timestamp":"2026-11-18T20:42:56.245Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-fixorder/test/yang/clojure_collection_order_test.cljc","content":"(defn- strictly-ascending?\n  \"True when `ks` sorts strictly ascending by jing/canonical-compare: every\n   adjacent pair compares negative. The strict form deliberately does NOT\n   certify a tie (equal adjacent keys are equal executable content and a\n   legal emitted order, but not a strictly ascending one) -- blocks that\n   construct a tie assert it directly or compare against the sequence's\n   own non-descending sort instead.\"\n  [ks]\n  (every? (fn [[a b]] (neg? (jing/canonical-compare a b)))\n          (partition 2 1 ks)))\n\n(defn- key-literals","numLines":12,"startLine":85,"totalLines":1095}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"call_00_ET_5g1UM9TS6nA4609i9P902849","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
